# What goes into the Docker build context. Only the two folders the Dockerfile copies are let in, so
# the upload to the daemon stays small and a change anywhere else (docs, notes, local tools) cannot
# invalidate a cached layer. A new COPY in the Dockerfile needs its folder allowed here as well.
# Docker reads the rules from top to bottom and the last matching one wins; * matches the top level
# only, ** matches at any depth.

# ── Only what the Dockerfile copies ──
*
# Stage "frontend": COPY frontend/
!frontend
# Stage "backend": COPY backend/AniLink.Api/ (the solution file and anything else beside it stays out)
!backend
backend/*
!backend/AniLink.Api

# ── Inside them: build output and installed packages are produced in the image ──
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.angular
**/coverage
# A frontend build that is copied next to the backend for local runs; the image takes its own from stage "frontend"
backend/**/wwwroot

# ── Local state, secrets and IDE files must never end up in an image layer ──
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Case-sensitive on the Linux builder, so both spellings are listed
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/*.local.json
**/.idea
**/.vs
**/*.user

# ── Notes and docs are not part of the image, and editing one must not rebuild the frontend ──
**/*.md
